# sec-fa workflow .flow format
#
# Workflow specs are authored as line-oriented `.flow` files. The format is
# intentionally not JSON, XML, YAML, or a programming language. Each nonblank
# line starts with one directive. `#` starts a comment outside quoted strings.
#
# Top-level directives:
#   workflow <name>
#   driver <driver_id>
#   mode <halted|observe|shadow|stage|paper|live_limited|live>
#   decision_as_of <UTC-instant>
#   allow_external_write <true|false>
#   allow_broker_resource <true|false>
#   layer <layer> [parent <parent_layer>] key <field>...
#   resource <id> <kind> [max_concurrent <n>] [min_interval_ms <n>] [allowed_modes <csv>] [hazard_class <A|B|C>]
#
# Node block:
#   node <node_id>
#     alg <algorithm_id>
#     cell <layer> <key=value>...
#     input <role> from <node_id>.<role>
#     set <config_key> <value>
#     output <role> <product_type>
#   end
#
# Values are parsed as bool, integer, float, or string in that order.
# Quote strings with spaces. Cell keys and config are canonicalized internally
# before hashing, but the authoritative workflow surface is this `.flow` text.
